 "topics": [
  {
   "topic": "Authority and consistency rules for conflicting ProjectValidationResult fields when creating grants or assignments",
   "members": [
    "r2.00",
    "r3.00"
   ],
   "runs": [
    2,
    3
   ],
   "questions": [
    "When `ProjectValidationResult.exists` or `is_active` disagrees with `status`, which facts decide whether a grant or assignment may be created?",
    "For grant and assignment creation, are `exists` and `is_active` authoritative, is `status` authoritative, or must ProjectValidationResult guarantee that these fields can never disagree?"
   ],
   "units": [
    "01_models.md:Model M17 — ProjectContext"
   ],
   "witnessed_by": [
    "r2.00",
    "r3.00"
   ],
   "id": "T1",
   "judgement": {
    "kind": "answered_later",
    "quotes": [
     "the grant and assignment operations of\naccess management read `exists` and `is_active` instead (A6, State 1 M17)\nand proceed only when both are true: `exists` false is refused as an\nunknown project, otherwise `is_active` false as an archived one",
     "A decoded validation answer is returned as it is and read by\nits caller as A5 says; the two readings of A5 agree, because the Registry\nsets `is_active = true` exactly when `status` is `active` (Registry v1\n`validate_project_reference`). The portal does not check the fields of an\nanswer against each other: each caller acts on the field A5 names for it,\nwhatever the others say"
    ],
    "later_state": null,
    "divergence": "",
    "why": "State 2 decides that grant and assignment creation uses `exists` and `is_active`, while Registry guarantees consistency with `status` and the portal performs no additional cross-field check.",
    "verified": true,
    "witness": {
     "outcomes": [
      "",
      ""
     ]
    },
    "blocking": false
   }
  }
 ],
